    "result_text": "The `AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class (the others are the abstract base and a capture helper). The full build passes: **BUILD SUCCESS**, all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` derivation on the Owner resource, following the existing pattern for derived read-only fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipTier`, etc.).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`LocalityResolver.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, single-responsibility, stateless helper in `rest.validation` (alongside the existing `AddressNormalizer`/`TelephoneNormalizer` transforms used by the mapper). It holds the fixed city-to-region table (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`) and returns the canonical region, or `\"UNKNOWN\"` for any other (or null) city.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `locality` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and it's documented in the API contract.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired the derivation into `toOwnerDto` via a computed `@Mapping` that delegates to `LocalityResolver.resolve(owner.getCity())`, exactly mirroring how the other derived fields are mapped. The mapper only delegates; the lookup logic lives in its own unit and is reusable (the region concept is also referenced by the postcode/timezone rules per the test's reference data).\n\n`locality` is a pure projection computed at DTO-mapping time \u2014 never persisted \u2014 consistent with the other derived owner fields.",
